  "passage": {
    "text": "Sometimes things go wrong in logistics. Last month a truck arrived at a shop with damaged boxes. The customer was angry and sent a complaint. The manager apologized and asked the driver what happened. The road was wet, and the driver braked hard. The company paid for the damage and the customer got a new shipment. The manager also made a new rule: drivers must tie the boxes more carefully. A problem is a chance to learn. Good managers do not blame people. They look for the reason and find a solution.",
    "cloze": true,
